{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/165654-resurrection-merits","id":165654,"title":"Resurrection Merits","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-10T22:50:16-07:00","id":165654,"title":"Resurrection Merits","content":"So I was inspired by the body hopping resurrection idea, what about a special set of merits for sin-eaters that change how or in what condition they come back?<br /> <br /> Body hopping, if nothing else, would extend a sin-eater's longevity since if they can go a while without resurrection they can hold off dying from old age for example.<br /> <br /> I get the feeling that quite a few people would like undead sin-eaters, so how about a collection of merits that make the sin-eater more revenant like? <br /> <br /> Or how about for a powerful sin-eater with a high ceremonies score with the &quot;hidden death&quot; merit, that they've enacted a ritual so that instead of a killing someone when they are killed, they foist their death on an inanimate object, which not being really alive in the first place, is fine to be used again, but if someone has your hidden death you're screwed.<br /> <br /> An idea I had that might be too gonzo is a sin-eater that has entwined their own soul with that of the their geist that their symbiosis is soul to soul without needing the medium of a body? Geist-Ghost hybrids as the new wraiths of the setting, but instead of being another splat as proposed before they are just sin-eaters with a series of merits like &quot;dematerialize&quot; or whatever other ghost traits one would like to tack onto a sin-eater. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T14:43:44-07:00","id":166239,"title":"","content":"I like the general idea (of course I do; something I wrote inspired it :-p)<br /> <br /> I would put Body-Jumping at a 4-dot Merit. Seems about right to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T22:15:34-07:00","id":166627,"title":"","content":"Now my thought about a sin-eater becoming more ghost like comes from this: Sin-eater already have ectoplasm running through their veins (in addition to blood), and are required to spend more and more time in the underworld. So what if they replaced more and more of their bodies with ectoplasm?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T03:03:24-07:00","id":166788,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/165654-resurrection-merits#post165654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or how about for a powerful sin-eater with a high ceremonies score with the &quot;hidden death&quot; merit, that they've enacted a ritual so that instead of a killing someone when they are killed, they foist their death on an inanimate object, which not being really alive in the first place, is fine to be used again, but if someone has your hidden death you're screwed.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>So kinda like a Lich's Phylactery? I am likeing where this thread is going already!<br /> How about one where they're dropped X (X = Psyche) rivers deep in the Underworld, and have to find their way back? Or perhaps one where they're dumped in the palace of some Deathlord, and have to perform some task for the Deathlord, in order to ressurrect? If you wanted to spice it up, you could put a time limit on how long time they had before it was too late. Maybe 2*X days?<br /> This thread has potential.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T23:04:31-07:00","id":167607,"title":"","content":"Well yes, like a lich's phylactory. Since Amechra's initial idea blurred the line between sin-eater and body thief, it seems only natural that a merit to blur the line between sin-eater and an eternal too.<br /> <br /> Those kind of seem like flaws, Krobeles, not merits, unless you put some nice benefits to it. I don't know if you intended it, but it kind of reminds me of Mummies. Perhaps something like &quot;Ordeal not Sacrifice&quot; so instead of taking a synergy hit the sin-eater has to earn their way back: if they're lucky they can keep coming back forever, if not they might not even get the 5 resurrections other sin-eaters get. <br /> <br /> Hmm, how about a vampire like resurrection merit? The core book talks about sin-eaters that replenish their plasm by drinking the ectoplasmic laced blood of other sin-eaters, and it would be in theme too.<br /> <br /> Ghosts can possess other bodies ala Intruders (which goes well with the body snatcher idea), but they can also possess other people as the vampiric bhuta, and I suppose the phylactory like merit would be seen as a take off of a fetter in this light. <br /> <br /> Anyway it seems to me that sin-eater seems like it should be rather broad, like changeling or mage, so that if a ST wants a vampire cult to be say a sin-eater and his bhuta minions instead of kindred there shouldn't be a problem with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T03:42:37-07:00","id":167718,"title":"","content":"The general idea was that the Sin-Eater didn't loose Synergy, not current nor maximum, but had to earn her way back, yes. Sorry if that didn't quite come off properly.<br /> I like the idea with the vampiric-sin-eater. How about they come back as the Revenants described on page 116 of Book of the Dead? They are extreamly hard to kill quasi-undead who have 1 lunar month, before they're sent screaming back into the depths of the great dark below? The required amount of Sin-Eater blood could be 10 &quot;doses of blood&quot; per point of Psyche the Sin-Eater has?<br /> Alternatively, the Sin-Eater could eat ghosts too, and the requirement could be 10 ranks of ghosts, per point of Psyche? This means its either a few Sin-Eaters, or a whole slur of ghosts.<br /> It seems alittle like a flaw at first glance, but being practically immortal is not be snuffed at.<br /> <br /> Or were you thinking more of a permanent &quot;they need to drink blood to live&quot; kinda thing?<br /> <br /> What about a merit that simply allowed the Sin-Eater to choose the victim of the forced death herself? Then instead of Thomas, the loving farther and devoted husband, dying, she could instead choose Jimmy. The scummy low-life from the slums who just last week, shived an old lady for her purse? Mechanically, I would say this could course the Sin-Eater to got drop 1 dot of Synergy, but just have her max reduced by 2, as normal. Since the Sin-Eater chose the victim herself, only her soul is torn as it asways is. Not the current relationship.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T07:22:29-07:00","id":167895,"title":"","content":"For the vampiric sin-eaters, I was thinking they could subsist on blood instead of food, but would not get plasm unless they ate a ghost or the blood of a fellow sin-eater.<br /> <br /> While of course anyone can do anything they like in their games, I wasn't thinking about making sin-eaters far more powerful, just give them some extra flavoring. <br /> <br /> So for revenant traits it would be stuff like &quot;don't need to eat, sleep, or breath,&quot; etc, not &quot;I've got the powers of the Crow and manifestations, eat it!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T20:36:52-07:00","id":168549,"title":"","content":"Perhaps note that they can transfer vampiric Vitae to Plasm by drinking Kindred blood, too. Or that could be a separate Merit, come to think, to allow for maximum flexibility.<br /> <br /> Other ideas:<br /> <br /> Purified!Sin-eaters: can now see and target Spirits with some powers (presumably, this would assume Geists are in fact ghost/spirit hybrids, as per the popular theory.) On the other hand, you resurrect in the Shadow and have to fight your way back.<br /> <br /> Promethean!Sin-eaters: died, came back &quot;on the operating table&quot; (perhaps literally.) Lose maximum Psyche, not Synergy, in a burst of Plasm (like Prometheans do when they resurrect.) Possibly some mad-scientist Merits allowing you to pin ghosts into human bodies in twisted semblance of life. The downside being, of course, that you were clearly not *meant* to come back - it was forced in some way by a freak of medical technology, and you are Bad and Unnatural for everything Sin-eaters are supposed to regulate, so get ready for pseudo-Wasteland and pseudo-Disquiet when others notice.<br /> <br /> Changeling!Sin-eaters: stayed dead for longer than usual, went deeper into the underworld, but escaped their tyrannical Deathlord by bargaining with a Geist. I have no idea what benefits this would provide -something to do with Bans? - but obviously their Underworld!Keeper wants them back.<br /> <br /> Mage!Sin-eaters: actually, this seems to be already covered.<br /> <br /> Vampire!Sin-eaters: the *other* side of vampires is the whole sex/addiction angle. Dracula, traditionally, is brought back by a giggling, stunted madman spilling his blood on the MAster's ashes. So, a Merit that makes your presence addictive, and allows your thralls (modified Retainers) to sacrifice themselves instead of the usual someone-dies-in-your-stead. On the other hand, these ties need to be maintained, and without them ... nobody's bringing you back.<br /> <br /> Ghost!Sin-eaters: beyond the obvious, I mean. Come back &quot;on your own&quot; via Anchors, instead of the usual Geist-based way. But aren't you damaging yourself by deliberately holding on to these things? Aren't Anchors meant to be released? Yes, yes they are, although I'm not sure how to represent that mechanically.<br /> <br /> Demon!Sin-eaters: The deal-with-the-devil angle. You already made a deal with your Geist. Why not ... make another deal? At least it doesn't involve killing anyone ... um, will it?<br /> <br /> Werewolf!Sin-eaters: guarding the borders of death is a dangerous job, and Sin-eaters get into a lot of fights. All Sin-eaters can heal injuries very effectively already; but these guys get a full-on, Wolverine-style healing factor. This is going to be expensive - perhaps some sort of rage-based drawback, courtesy of a Geist that is clearly expecting combat - but on the other hand, if they actually manage to die then there's no coming back from that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":877,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","user":"MugaSofer","date":". 06-13-2014, 11:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T03:55:16-07:00","id":168758,"title":"","content":"Hmm, those are some interesting ideas.<br /> <br /> For spiritual sin-eaters ala the purified, instead of manifesting in the hisil, I'd make it that the geist has to absorb enough essence to repair the body, either from absorbing essence that reflects their nature or from sacrifices in their name, religious style, since I wouldn't these guys losing synergy it would have to be limited in another way so it's not just a &quot;resurrect again and again for free&quot; thing. Not what I'm proposing here after all.<br /> <br /> Promethean style sin-eaters wouldn't need so much work actually, they'd just have to make them the result of one of those vacant sin-eaters managing to successfully binding a geist against its will, but by doing so they opened a hole between life and death, for a wasteland like effect, and they come back through their binding of the geist, since the geist normally would be thrilled to leave them to die.<br /> <br /> For changeling style sin-eaters, I'd have sin-eater mutants, the ectoplasm didn't just flow through their blood, but actually manifests as physical mutations, probably in accordance with their geist's nature. So I'd guess these guys would be avatars, seemingly normal to those without unseen senses-ghosts, but walking gods of death to those who can see such things. <br /> <br /> Demonic style sin-eaters, hmm, well it would seem more appropriate if they were sin-eaters that were able to become gestalt entities, tatterdemalions of souls. Collecting features from ghosts they've consumed or helped move on, when killed, they just slip into a patchwork life. A suicide's job, a mugging victim's apartment, a cancer patient's parents, etc. Ghosts bring them new life, and in return the ghosts live vicariously through the sin-eater. Or if you wanted to go entirely predatory a sin-eater that can come back as a dead person by feeding them to their geist that would be a real synergy sin I'd imagine. <br /> <br /> Werewolf like sin-eaters I'd go for canine guardians of the dead: cerberus, church grims, I'd make it sin-eaters who can manifest an ectoplasmic covering in canid form. While I haven't play tested it, against ghost based threats I don't think sin-eaters need much pumping up really.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T06:10:51-07:00","id":168839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/165654-resurrection-merits?p=168758#post168758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For spiritual sin-eaters ala the purified, instead of manifesting in the hisil, I'd make it that the geist has to absorb enough essence to repair the body, either from absorbing essence that reflects their nature or from sacrifices in their name, religious style, since I wouldn't these guys losing synergy it would have to be limited in another way so it's not just a &quot;resurrect again and again for free&quot; thing. Not what I'm proposing here after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>.I figure the restricting element is fighting your way through the Shadow - you have a chance to get eaten by a Spirit, basically.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Promethean style sin-eaters wouldn't need so much work actually, they'd just have to make them the result of one of those vacant sin-eaters managing to successfully binding a geist against its will, but by doing so they opened a hole between life and death, for a wasteland like effect, and they come back through their binding of the geist, since the geist normally would be thrilled to leave them to die.<br /> <br /> For changeling style sin-eaters, I'd have sin-eater mutants, the ectoplasm didn't just flow through their blood, but actually manifests as <u>physical mutations</u>, probably in accordance with their geist's nature. So I'd guess these guys would be avatars, seemingly normal to those without unseen senses-ghosts, but walking gods of death to those who can see such things. </div> </div> </div>That's an interesting idea - I considered it for werewolf!geist, actually, but I'm not sure how well it would tie in with a Resurrection Merit.<br /> <br /> It seems oddly fitting for promethean, patchwork-people style mad scientist immortality, come to think. And of course, Changelings were tortured and reshaped ...<br /> <br /> OK, two versions: one where you feel your death(s), retaining marks and such (but physical/mental ones, not damaged &quot;soul&quot;/Synergy.) Another where you are artificial, and can <i>potentially</i> do the same (awful) thing to others with mad science.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Demonic style sin-eaters, hmm, well it would seem more appropriate if they were sin-eaters that were able to become gestalt entities, tatterdemalions of souls. Collecting features from ghosts they've consumed or helped move on, when killed, they just slip into a patchwork life. A suicide's job, a mugging victim's apartment, a cancer patient's parents, etc. Ghosts bring them new life, and in return the ghosts live vicariously through the sin-eater. Or if you wanted to go entirely predatory a sin-eater that can come back as a dead person by feeding them to their geist that would be a real synergy sin I'd imagine. </div> </div> </div>There are a whole bunch of Ephemeral Entities out there, and they can all purchase the Resurrection Numen. I figure the precise payment would be left relatively open, with various options suggested.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Werewolf like sin-eaters I'd go for canine guardians of the dead: cerberus, church grims, I'd make it sin-eaters who can manifest an ectoplasmic covering in canid form. While I haven't play tested it, against ghost based threats I don't think sin-eaters need much pumping up really. </div> </div> </div>Indeed. Perhaps more emphasis on the other side - stopping the living (including other supernaturals) from meddling where they don't belong. A sort of metaphorical Cerberus-esque guardian of the underworld is what I had in mind, yeah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}